# Feature branches

Before starting a **new feature or non-trivial change**, create and check out a branch first.

## Convention

- Prefix: `cursor/` (e.g. `cursor/trace`, `cursor/specs-expand`)
- Name: short kebab-case describing the work
- Base: latest `master` (pull/rebase if needed)

## Workflow

1. Remind the user (or just do it when they ask to start work): create `cursor/<feature>` from `master`.
2. Implement and commit on that branch.
3. Merge to `master` (and push) only when the user asks.

## Do not

- Commit feature work directly on `master` unless the user explicitly requests a hotfix on `master`.
- Leave large WIP only in `git stash` when a branch would be clearer — prefer a branch.
